# Alt–aug–regal on a jewel: the cheap opener for small mod pools.
#
# A jewel holds two prefixes and two suffixes, so a guide rolls it with Orbs of
# Alteration until the wanted prefix appears with the suffix side still empty,
# adds a suffix with an Orb of Augmentation, and only then spends a Regal Orb.
# Alterations are cheap; the Regal is the one roll that cannot be retried, so
# the guide takes it only once two of the three wanted mods are in hand.

item {
    base:   "Viridian Jewel"
    ilvl:   84
    rarity: normal
}

def usefulSuffix() =
    has "fire damage over time multiplier"
    or has "attack speed with bows"
    or has "global critical strike multiplier"

transmute

# An alteration lays down one or two mods; wait for the life roll with nothing
# beside it, so the augment below is guaranteed a suffix slot.
until has "increased maximum life" and suffixCount == 0 {
    alteration
}

augment

# A bad suffix is not annulled (that could take the life); the guide goes back
# to rolling, which `restart` says exactly.
until usefulSuffix() {
    alteration
    if has "increased maximum life" and suffixCount == 0 {
        augment
    }
}

regal
